cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, or cite the values it establishes, please cite the archived version below."
title: "DiscrepancyRecords: a SAT campaign on the discrepancy-2 thresholds N(k,2)"
abstract: >-
  A SAT-based campaign on N(k,2), the least N such that every plus-minus-one
  coloring of {1..N} has an arithmetic progression with partial sum of absolute
  value at least 2 (Erdos problem #176, OEIS A398541). Lower bounds are avoiding
  colorings checkable without a solver; upper bounds must come from two
  structurally different encodings.
type: software
authors:
